      "summary": "A concurrent basis update from another API process can make an accept decision stale after authorization but before acceptance is recorded.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Persistence/CaseStateStore.cs",
          "line": 168,
          "message": "Acceptance authorization is not atomic across API processes. Protect the current-basis check and acceptance mutation against commits from other processes.",
          "confidence": 0.84,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "AcceptIfAuthorized checks the current decision inside WithCurrentState, which holds only this CaseStateStore instance's in-process lock. CaseStateStore commits also use a file lock, so another API process sharing the configured state file can commit a newer basis without taking this lock.",
            "failureScenario": "With two API processes sharing the state file, one process checks a current accept decision while the other commits a newer basis. The first process then records acceptance in CaseStore using the now-stale decision. This bypasses M-10's current-decision gate. OWASP A01:2025 Broken Access Control."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
